  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday morning through next Thursday)\nIssued at 255 PM EDT Fri Sep 11 2026\n\nBy Sunday morning the main frontal boundary from the short term will \nhave moved into central GA with a slightly drier airmass moving into \nNorth GA. Deep moisture from the Gulf will remain in place across \ncentral and south GA with diurnally driven storms expected. This \nfrontal boundary continue to move south clearing the area by Mon \nmorning. The drier airmass remain across the area through the middle \nof next week keeping precipitation chances at 20% or less each day \n(Mon-Thu).  \n\nTemps will stay in the upper 80s to middle 90s through day 7 but \nwith the drier airmass moving in Heat index values will slowly fall \nthrough the middle of next week. Dewpoints Sunday and Mon will be in \nthe lower to middle 70s but they will fall into the lower to middle \n60s by Wed. Even with temps still in the lower 90s it will feel a \nbit more comfortable.",
